      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): reject with AbortError when tool execution is cancelled",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen a tool execution is cancelled via the agent's AbortSignal, onAbortSignal calls run.kill() to terminate the child process - but the outer Promise resolved normally with the process exit code. The agent manager was misled into believing the tool finished normally.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe process exit handler (run.promise.then(...)) resolved the outer Promise with buildExecForegroundResult regardless of whether the exit was caused by an abort signal or natural completion. The fix adds a toolAborted flag set by onAbortSignal. When the exit handler fires after an abort, it rejects with DOMException(AbortError) instead of resolving.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Cancel/stop during bash tool execution now correctly aborts the agent run\n- Backgrounded and yielded sessions remain unaffected\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Before (buggy)\nonAbortSignal -> run.kill() -> run.promise resolves with exit code -> agent thinks tool succeeded\n\n### After (fixed)\nonAbortSignal -> toolAborted=true -> run.kill() -> run.promise rejects(AbortError) -> agent aborts run\n\n### Tests + lint\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/bash-tools.exec-host-shared.test.ts\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  28 passed (28)\n\n$ npx oxlint -c .oxlintrc.json src/agents/bash-tools.exec.ts -> No errors\n$ npx oxfmt --check src/agents/bash-tools.exec.ts -> All matched files use correct format\n```\n\n## What Changed\n\n- src/agents/bash-tools.exec.ts: +6 lines (toolAborted flag + AbortError rejection)\n\nFixes #105681\n\n## AI Assistance\n- AI-assisted: Yes\n- Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n- Human confirmed understanding: Yes",
